column134:
23/Sep/17 7:28 PM;557058:f99670ac-6f0b-469b-bdfb-a9817a67932f;The tag select is empty because we do this:

https://github.com/otwcode/otwarchive/blob/86f6e8af2d781efb06617da8d9782765b0365cdd/app/controllers/admin_posts_controller.rb#L17
{code}
@tags = AdminPostTag.where(language_id: @language.id).order(:name)
{code}

but none of the admin post tags have languages.

Instead, Sarken said we should get all the tags from all the admin posts in language, like:
{code}
@tags = AdminPostTag.joins(:admin_posts).where(admin_posts: {language_id: @language.id})
{code}

column141:
13/Mar/19 1:50 PM;557058:443ab871-4096-403e-bd6f-f3534fe417f0;Fields are now marked using approach number three! Looks good.

If we don't have one, though, we should make an issue for the fact that the labels and form fields are not properly associated -- that is, if I click on "How many invitations would you like? (max 10)*", it does not put focus on the associated input. I think it's because the labels are (and have always been) coded incorrectly -- they're


{code:ruby}
<%= f.label ts("How many invitations would you like? (max %{max})", :max => ArchiveConfig.MAX_USER_INVITE_REQUEST.to_s) %>
{code}


when they should be

{code:ruby}
<%= f.label :quantity, ts("How many invitations would you like? (max %{max})", :max => ArchiveConfig.MAX_USER_INVITE_REQUEST.to_s) %>
{code}

