column134:
23/Sep/21 6:40 PM;557058:443ab871-4096-403e-bd6f-f3534fe417f0;h2. NoMethodError in ArchiveFaqs#index

Showing _otwarchive/app/views/archive_faqs/_filters.html.erb_ where line *#7* raised:

{noformat}undefined method `name' for nil:NilClass{noformat}

{noformat}<%= select_tag :language_id, ('<option></option>' + options_from_collection_for_select(available_faq_locales, :iso, :name, params[:language_id])).html_safe %>{noformat}

Why? Because:

{noformat}def available_faq_locales
  ArchiveFaq.translated_locales.map { |code| Locale.find_by(iso: code) }
end{noformat}

If we change a locale’s ISO – which is definitely something we want to be able to do; looking at you, {{UKR}} instead of {{uk}} – we need to also update the locales of {{archive_faq_translations}} and {{question_translations}}

column30:
The README on our Github repo currently includes the following text:

{code:java}
* Bug Tracking: https://code.google.com/p/otwarchive/issues/list
{code}

This should be changed as follows:

{code}
* Bug Tracking: https://otwarchive.atlassian.net/projects/AO3/issues
{code}

With "https://otwarchive.atlassian.net/projects/AO3/issues" being a link to the same.

h1. Steps to reproduce
1. Log in
2. Hi, username > My Dashboard > Skins > My Work Skins > Create Work Skin
3. Fill in required fields and attempt to use CSS like

{noformat}
.sms span::before { 
  clip: rect(1.1em, 1.94em, 2.33em, 0); 
  transform: rotatey(180deg);
}
{noformat}

4. Submit
5. Get an error message like

{noformat}
Sorry! We couldn't save this skin because:
  * The clip property in .sms span::before cannot have the value rect(1.1em, 1.94em, 2.33em, 0), sorry!
  * The transform property in .sms span::before cannot have the value rotatey(180deg), sorry!
{noformat}

h1. Expected results
1. For the clip property, I expect to be able to use a value in the form of rect(top, right, bottom, left)
2. For the transform property, I expect to be able to use a value in the form of rotatex(angle) or rotatey(angle) -- it currently only takes rotate(angle)

h1. Further testing notes
You can use the following skin CSS and work HTML if you have the burning desire to see the properties in action:

h2. Skin CSS

{noformat}
#workskin .ios8 {
  display: block;
  font-family: "Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  width: 19em;
  margin: 0.625em auto;
}

#workskin .ios8 .message {
  border-radius: 1.25em;
  display: inline-block;
  font-family: "Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  line-height: 1;
  padding: 0.625em 0.75em;
  position: relative;
}

#workskin .ios8 span::before {
  border-radius: 50% 50% 50% 50%;
  border-style: solid;
  border-width: 0 1.1em;
  bottom: 0;
  clip: rect(1.1em, 1.94em, 2.33em, 0);
  content: " ";
  height: 2.2em;
  position: absolute;
  width: 1.66em;
  z-index: -1;
}

#workskin .mine.ios8 {
  text-align: right;
}

#workskin .yours.ios8 {
  text-align: left;
}

#workskin .mine.ios8 span::before {
  border-color: #43b4fb;
  right: -2.7em;
}

#workskin .yours.ios8 span::before {
  border-color: #e5e5ea;
  left: -2.7em;
  transform: rotatey(180deg);
}

#workskin .mine.ios8 .message {
  background: #43b4fb;
  color: #fff;
  margin-right: 0;
}

#workskin .yours.ios8 .message {
  background: #e5e5ea;
  color: #000;
  margin-left: 0;
}
{noformat}


h2. Work HTML


{noformat}
<p class="mine ios8 skin hidden">
  <span class="message">This is my first sent text</span>
</p>

<p class="mine ios8 skin hidden">
  <span class="message">This is the second text message I'm sending in a row with my iPhone happy happy joy joy</span>
</p>

<p class="yours ios8 skin hidden">
  <span class="message">This is someones' reply</span>
</p>

<p class="mine ios8 skin hidden">
  <span class="message">I'm :)ing</span>
</p>

<p class="yours ios8 skin hidden">
  <span class="message">Here is a reply from someone else</span>
</p>

<p class="yours ios8 skin hidden">
  <span class="message">Their second reply in a row</span>
</p>
{noformat}

