column30:
Create a work with <pre> tags with immediate child tags in the chapter text:

{code:none}<pre><code>This is preformatted code with multiple lines</code></pre>{code}

h2. What happens

The parser turns it into multiline formatted html

{code:none}<pre>
   <code>This is preformatted code with multiple lines</code>
</pre>{code}

which gets rendered with the extra spaces at the start of the line:

{code:none} This is preformatted code with multiple lines{code}

defeating the purpose of the {{PRE}} tag.

h2. What should happen

The HTML tags should stay the same, with the same whitespace, even after editing and saving multiple times:

{noformat}<pre><code>This is preformatted code with multiple lines</code></pre>{noformat}

