column133:
20/Apr/17 7:33 PM;557058:f99670ac-6f0b-469b-bdfb-a9817a67932f;I can reproduce this on the work posting form. This should affect everywhere we use tokeninput.

The problem is this part:

{code:js}
    // Highlight the query part of the search term
    function highlight_term(value, term) {
        var newvalue = value;
        $.each(term.split(' '), function(index, termbit) {
            termbit = termbit.replace(/([.?*+^$[\]\\(){}-])/g, "\\$1");            
            newvalue = newvalue.replace(new RegExp("(?![^&;]+;)(?!<[^<>]*)(" + termbit + ")(?![^<>]*>)(?![^&;]+;)", "gi"), "<b>$1</b>");
        });
        return newvalue;
    }
{code}

The extra space is crucial, and it doesn't have to be at the end of the input. It can be at the start, it can be two spaces next to each other, so long as the results when we split the term include an empty string.

{code:js}
'fine '.split(' ') // ['fine', '']
' fine'.split(' ') // ['', 'fine']
'fine  '.split(' ') // ['fine', '', '']
{code}

When we use the empty string for the final replace, this happens:

{code}
Term: "fine ", value: "Fine &amp; Dandy"
Term: "fine ", value: "<b><b></b>F<b></b>i<b></b>n<b></b>e</b><b></b> <b></b>&amp<b></b>;<b></b> <b></b>D<b></b>a<b></b>n<b></b>d<b></b>y<b></b>"
{code}

One pair of b tags manages to get between "&amp" and ";". Browsers can read the imperfect "&amp" as an entity and display "&", leaving us with ";".

We can fix this by skipping over empty termbits.
